{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Performance"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record is data the linker places in a section, so nothing runs for it at launch. Reading a set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"walks every loaded image’s section once and calls the accessor of each record of the set’s kind."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That’s linear in the records the program holds, and the reads aren’t cached, so read a set once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where the program starts and keep the array. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsPerformanceTests"},{"type":"text","text":" checks the scaling in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"release builds: reading 3,000 records costs no more than about 10 times reading 300."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The build pays for each marked declaration: the macro’s expansion and the record it compiles to."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That cost is also linear while the records are spread across files, as they are in an app."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thousands of records in one file take the compiler much longer, so generated registries are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"better split."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Measured","anchor":"Measured","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":" measures both in a SwiftPM package of generated records, against the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declarations without the macro. These figures are from an M1 Ultra with Swift 6.4.2, in a debug"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build, with each size’s records split across 10 files:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","alignments":["right","right","right","right"],"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Records","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Build time the records add","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per record"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading every record (release)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"100"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.6 s"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"26 ms"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"77 µs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.2 s","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 ms"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"242 µs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"10,000","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"50 s"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"5.0 ms","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2.0 ms","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The 100-record row is mostly the macro plugin’s start-up, paid once per module that uses it. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read also has a fixed part, the walk over every image the process has loaded, which is about","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"70 µs on macOS. In a single file, 10,000 records added 111 s to the build instead of 50 s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"role":"article","title":"Unique keys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article","title":"What the macros refuse"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","title":"Declaring a kind","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"role":"article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"}}}